---
import '../styles/inner.css';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy — EV Chandigarh"
  description="How we research and source what we publish, who reviews it, how to report a mistake, and why we stay independent of the people who sell vehicles."
  type="website"
>
  <section class="page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <Eyebrow text="Editorial policy" />
      <h1 class="page-title disp">How we work, and how to hold us to it</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">Accuracy and independence are the only things this publication has to offer. This page sets out, plainly, how we try to earn both — and how to tell us when we get it wrong.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="page-body prose">
      <h2>How we research and source</h2>
      <p>Every factual claim — a tariff, a registration rule, a subsidy deadline, a spec — is checked against a primary or near-primary source: the relevant regulation (for example the Central Motor Vehicles Rules), the electricity regulator's tariff order, the manufacturer's own listing, or established reporting. Where a figure is a range or varies by variant, state or time, we say so rather than pretending a single number is universal.</p>
      <p>We date our facts. Anything time-sensitive — electricity tariffs, subsidy windows, prices — carries the period it was verified, and we re-check those figures periodically. If we can't verify something to our own satisfaction, we don't publish it as fact.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Who reviews it</h2>
      <p>Articles are written and then reviewed by a named person before publication, and every page shows who wrote it and who reviewed it, with the dates it was published and last updated. That attribution isn't decoration — it's us putting our names to the work so you know who stands behind it.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Corrections — how to report a mistake</h2>
      <p>We will get things wrong, and when we do we fix them on the record. If you spot an error — a number that's out of date, a rule we've misread, a claim that doesn't hold — tell us, and we'll check it against the source and correct it promptly. Material corrections are reflected in the article's "Updated" date so the change is visible, not quietly buried.</p>
      <p>To report an error, reach us on WhatsApp or at our contact address (see <a href="/about">About</a>). Please include the page and the specific claim so we can verify it quickly.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Our independence</h2>
      <p><strong>We don't sell vehicles.</strong> EV Chandigarh publishes information, not inventory — no prices, no bookings, no dealer pages. When you're ready to buy, we route you to where you can: our commerce partner at <a href="https://evchandigarh.com" rel="noopener">evchandigarh.com</a> and a WhatsApp line. Keeping the buying separate from the explaining is what lets our guidance stay neutral.</p>
      <p>We write about a category, not a catalogue. When a specific model is the clearest way to illustrate a point, we name it as an example of its class — never as "our" product to push.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
